@ [residual_registry] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\CPMS_I03C_Semantic_Residual_Registry.sop

& [Purpose] produce two inspectable observations over one root-qualified subject
  + schema reader asks whether a JSON value satisfies the exact I02 Draft 2020-12 document
  + typed reader asks whether the actual Rust root can deserialize or serialize the subject
  + neither observation implies semantic validity authority admission compatibility or effect permission
  + disagreement is preserved as evidence rather than reconciled by preference

& [Prerequisites] are exact and non-substitutive
  + I03A exact validator dependency activation is required before validator implementation
  + I03B faithful byte ingress pass is required before either input reader runs
  + I03C residual registry identity is required before observation results may carry residual references
  + formation may define this contract while every prerequisite implementation remains inactive

& [RootBindings] are exact
  + prepare_input input_deserialize PrepareRequest
  + run_input input_deserialize PreparedRunRequest
  + verify_input input_deserialize VerifyRequest
  + base_response output_serialize ProcedureToolResponse under base-response intended use
  + preparation_response output_serialize ProcedureToolResponse under preparation-response intended use
  + the response roots remain distinct even though they share a Rust type and materially similar schema payloads

& [ReaderIndependence] is structural
  + both branches bind the same root document digest and subject digest
  + schema reader materializes its own serde_json Value only after I03B acceptance
  + typed input reader deserializes the actual Rust type from the original retained bytes rather than from schema reader Value
  + output typed reader serializes an admitted typed fixture before the resulting bytes pass I03B and schema observation
  + no branch consumes transforms filters or repairs the other branch result

& [InputFlow] is fixed
  * bind root exact document faithful instance and registry
  * independently parse exact retained bytes to schema-reader Value
  * independently deserialize exact retained bytes to the actual root type and require deserializer end
  * validate schema-reader Value against the bound validator
  * normalize both observations without comparing them

& [OutputFlow] is fixed
  * bind root intended-use fixture exact document and registry
  * serialize actual ProcedureToolResponse to exact bytes
  * require repeat serialization byte equality
  * run faithful byte ingress over produced bytes
  * materialize schema-reader Value and validate the bound document
  * emit typed serialization and schema observations without claiming intended-use semantics

& [ReaderDisposition] is accepted rejected exhausted internal_fault not_applicable or skipped_dependency
  + accepted or rejected means the applicable reader completed its own declared operation
  + exhausted means a finite finding representation numeric or recursion capacity prevented completion
  + not_applicable means an earlier applicability rule intentionally excludes the reader
  + skipped_dependency means a required inactive or absent prerequisite and blocks proof
  + internal_fault means an invariant or unexpected reader failure and blocks proof

& [ObservationStage] is binding representation validation deserialization serialization completion or normalization
  + disposition and stage are both required
  + schema representation refusal is not schema rejection
  + typed deserialization refusal is not semantic refusal

& [ValidatorProfile] is exact candidate jsonschema 0.49.2 with default features false
  + Draft 2020-12 is explicit
  + document dialect id digest closure and local reference preflight precede construction
  + no HTTP HTTPS file environment registry caller resolver async or external resource retriever
  + every reference must be an in-document fragment whose target exists
  + meta-schema observation construction and instance validation remain distinct results

& [FormatPolicy] is Draft 2020-12 annotation only
  + no custom format assertion is registered
  + exact I02 format values are int64 uint32 and uint64
  + typed Rust decoding rather than schema format annotation enforces destination integer representation
  + schema acceptance plus typed rejection on an out-of-range integer is a legitimate reader disagreement

& [SchemaRepresentation] is bounded serde_json Value
  + source digest remains the I03B exact-byte digest
  + value projection digest uses canonical sorted-object JSON bytes and is separate from source digest
  + I03B numeric token spans remain attached to observation evidence
  + value parse syntax or EOF failure after I03B acceptance is internal_fault
  + a valid number outside the selected Value representation is exhausted at representation stage and never schema_rejected

& [ExactI02KeywordInventory] is closed at the I02 bundle baseline
  + structural and annotation keys are dollar defs dollar id dollar ref dollar schema items patternProperties properties required title and format
  + instance-rejection rule classes are additional_properties any_of constant enum maximum minimum maximum_length minimum_length one_of pattern required type and unique_items
  + reference failure after preflight is internal_fault
  + pattern backtrack limit is exhausted and regex engine failure is internal_fault
  + format never emits a finding under annotation-only policy
  + any previously unseen validator error kind is profile_drift internal_fault rather than an invented stable class

& [SchemaFinding] carries stable owned evidence only
  + finding id root document digest instance digest rule class instance path schema path evaluation path optional absolute keyword location and rule context digest
  + rule context owns exact bounded fields such as unexpected properties required property type set enum digest constant digest numeric or length limit and one-of branch status
  + engine Display Debug allocation addresses iterator order and prose are not identity
  + findings sort by instance path schema path evaluation path rule class context digest and finding id
  + maximum findings is 256 per observation
  + attempting finding 257 yields atomic exhausted observation and no accepted or rejected disposition

& [TypedInputReader] is exact
  + create serde_json Deserializer from original retained bytes
  + deserialize PrepareRequest PreparedRunRequest or VerifyRequest selected only by root binding
  + call end after typed value construction even though I03B already proved one complete JSON value
  + on success serialize the typed value to a normalized projection and retain projection digest and bytes account
  + normalized projection is not represented as the original spelling or a byte round trip

& [TypedOutputReader] is exact
  + input is an immutable OutputFixtureEnvelope carrying root fixture id fixture digest intended-use assertion and actual ProcedureToolResponse
  + base and preparation fixtures are never interchangeable by Rust type equality alone
  + serialize with serde_json to exact bytes and repeat once
  + byte mismatch is nondeterministic internal_fault
  + serializer failure is internal_fault unless an explicit finite byte bound is exhausted
  + intended-use assertion remains fixture evidence and is not proved by serialization

& [SerdeFaultNormalization] is stable and bounded
  + category is io syntax data or eof from serde_json Error classification
  + line and column are retained as exact reader locators under the locked serde_json version
  + bounded advisory message is not identity
  + input syntax or eof after I03B pass is cross_reader_internal_fault
  + input data is typed rejection
  + io is impossible for slice input and becomes internal_fault
  + no dependency is added for inferred typed paths in this profile

& [TypedProjection] carries root type name source digest projection digest projection byte length and no typed value in the durable observation
  + typed value remains an ephemeral local product
  + sensitive field content is not copied into diagnostics

& [SchemaObservation] carries profile root document digest source digest value projection digest disposition stage findings numeric token references accounts and observation digest
& [SerdeObservation] carries profile root type name source or fixture digest typed projection digest disposition stage normalized fault accounts and observation digest

& [ReaderPair] carries binding digest schema observation serde observation and pair digest
  + no agreement accepted refused pass compatible or authoritative field exists in I03D
  + I03E alone compares observations to case expectations and constructs findings

& [ResidualCarry] is referential
  + pair carries applicable residual ids resolved through I03C without changing their disposition
  + schema acceptance never removes typed semantic or authority residuals
  + reader rejection cannot create a new residual id from prose

& [Resources] are finite
  + input bytes and structural limits are inherited exactly from I03B
  + one schema Value projection maximum 16777216 bytes
  + one typed projection maximum 16777216 bytes
  + maximum findings 256 and maximum diagnostic characters 1024
  + maximum normalized path segments 128 and path characters 4096
  + every count and byte accumulation uses checked arithmetic

& [Atomicity] is strict
  + prerequisite identity failure emits one pair-construction fault and no ReaderPair
  + each reader observation is internally atomic
  + a completed reader observation remains preserved if its independent peer rejects or exhausts
  + pair cannot be emitted if root source document registry or binding identities disagree

& [FutureSourceTouch] is unsigned
  + modify crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/lib.rs under future schema-conformance feature
  + add crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/reader_observation.rs
  + add crates/cantor_procedure_tool/tests/reader_observation.rs
  + no Cargo change belongs to I03D because I03A owns dependency activation
  + no existing enforcement schema golden CLI MCP service ecosystem preflight provider model or effect file touch

& [ProofFamilies] are exact
  + five root bindings and both response intended uses
  + accepted and rejected schema and typed observations independently
  + missing unknown wrong type enum tag integer spelling and out-of-range numeric disagreement witnesses
  + exact paths rule classes context digests serde categories line columns projections and repeat equality
  + local reference success plus external missing and escaping reference preflight refusal
  + finding 255 256 and 257 boundaries projection byte boundaries and recursive representation exhaustion
  + mutation of root document source registry binding and observation digests
  + proof that no reader invokes semantic admission provider model service persistence network effect or hardware

& [Delineation] is exact
  - never: compare to corpus expectation claim agreement classify compatibility execute semantic enforcement admit authority invoke provider or model persist serve notify network effect produce release or target hardware FPGA

& [PresentDisposition] is source_preserved_formation_only_no_reader_authority
